# direnv config: while inside this repo, put its root on PATH so the ./remote
# helper (deploy / status / log, see `remote sync --help`) can be run as just
# `remote`. Takes effect in this directory and its subdirectories only, so it
# never touches your global shell config or PATH elsewhere.
#
# One-time activation per checkout (direnv refuses to auto-load until you trust
# the file). Every time the .envrc changed, direnv will ask you to do this to activate:
#   direnv allow

# adding the `tools`-directory to the PATH env-var
PATH_add tools

# initializing aliases + shell functions:
. .aliases
